    <refsection>
        <title>Conclusion</title>
        <para>
        On this page we compared the simulation results of generated FMUs. By analysing the results, we could say that the better solver for the FMUs ME is CVODE-BDF with FUNCTIONAL iterations. 
        For the FMUs CS we have almost the same value of errors for all kind of solvers, this is explained by the fact that the FMUs for Co-Simulation have there own solvers to perform numerical integration.
        All of the above results was obtained with the simulation that has been done with default parameters for the relative and absolute tolerances. 
        So, by configuring the parameters of the tolerance a user is able to reduce the simulation errors.  
    </para>
